CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.[0-9]*\] .* empty ls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.[0-9]*\] .* one ls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.[0-9]*\] .* nested expansion: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.[0-9]*\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The function parameter pack was sized like the FIRST template pack
(Js); its own pack's name was looked up in the instantiated declaration,
where a one-element pack is already replaced by its element.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
